     [38;5;246mPure validator module, plus a separate thin binder that wires a form element and renders errors. Forms can use [39m
     [38;5;246meither layer.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Validator only (pure)
     [38;5;246mCompute results; every form handles its own submit wiring and error display. Smallest surface, most repetition per
[39m     [38;5;246mform.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Validator + DOM binding, one module
     [38;5;246mSingle module that always owns submit handling and error rendering. Least per-form code, but no way to opt out of [39m
     [38;5;246mits markup conventions.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Rules declared in HTML attributes
     [38;5;246mdata-rules on inputs, module reads them. Least JS, but weak for cross-field and conditional rules.[39m
